+Zahir Uddin is a data and technology executive with more than 25 years building commercial data platforms, Master Data Management programs, and analytics organizations across pharma and life sciences. He spent over seven years in senior data and IT leadership at SK Life Science, Inc., culminating in the role of Head of IT (January 2024 - January 2026), where he owned the enterprise data and analytics ecosystem supporting $1 billion in annual commercial operations. That platform was built on Snowflake with curated bronze/silver/gold layers following a Medallion architecture pattern, feeding Power BI and, from a 2025 evaluation, Looker as the strategic semantic layer for governed self-service analytics.
+
+His background covers the core commercial data domains central to a Human Health data organization - HCP/HCO, patient claims, Rx, market access, specialty pharmacy, and CRM data - alongside direct ownership of data governance, cost management, and platform reliability at enterprise scale. He directed a governance model spanning HCP/HCO, Product, Vendor, Finance, and Commercial domains with formal change control embedded to meet GxP, SOX, and audit requirements, and sponsored production AI initiatives including agentic security automation and a Snowflake Cortex-built next-best-action model for Medical Affairs. As Head of Applications before that, he led the enterprise application and commercial data ecosystem through the company's first U.S. pharmaceutical launch. Zahir holds a Bachelor of Science in Information Systems from Brunel University London and is based in Montville, New Jersey.